; Flambda optimization level for release builds (the profile used by the
; Docker/production image). -O3 enables aggressive cross-module inlining,
; closure elimination and unboxing, which removes most of the per-event
; allocation on the execution-event hot path. It is a no-op on non-flambda
; compilers; the release profile must be built on a flambda switch (see
; Dockerfile).
;
; The dev profile needs -O2 for the same backend reason: without an explicit
; level the compiler keeps every value of the large [asset_domain_worker]
; function in its own stack slot, producing a 73KB frame. OxCaml's arm64
; emitter then prints that frame size with [movz] and the assembler rejects the
; >16-bit immediate. -O2 coalesces the slots (frame drops to ~3KB) and keeps
; local builds working; release stays at -O3.

(env
 (dev
  (ocamlopt_flags
   (:standard -O2)))
 (release
  (ocamlopt_flags
   (:standard -O3))))
